  <running_head>ΕΙΚΩΝ ΒΑΣΙΛΙΚΗ</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>feorsim</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">
      <i>mula</i> [?] obstipetur &amp; <i>torpeat</i> Spiritus precum</l>
    <l n="2">&amp; Devotionis, quàm, ne confusa &amp; im-</l>
    <l n="3">meditata varietas <i>distrahat</i> illum penitus,</l>
    <l n="4">vel <i>excludat</i>.</l>
    <l n="5" para="true">Quamquam verò haud repugnem</l>
    <l n="6">exerceri à Ministris <i>dona</i> sua, etiam in</l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>publico</i>, dum id graviter fiat &amp; humiliter,</l>
    <l n="8">&amp; eâ quâ decet prudentia, quo, &amp; sua</l>
    <l n="9">forsan magis &amp; Populi studia excitari</l>
    <l n="10">possint, &amp; in præsens negotium præpara-</l>
    <l n="11">ri; nulla suadet propterea necessitas,</l>
    <l n="12">ut quantacunque visingenii, &amp; eximiæ</l>
    <l n="13">dotes privatorum hominum, pellant</l>
    <l n="14">penitus ab Ecclesia, vel illi fraude</l>
    <l n="15">eripiant conjunctas facultates &amp; conf-</l>
    <l n="16">spirantia dona tot Doctrinæ &amp; pietatis</l>
    <l n="17">laude præstantium, quales erant, qui</l>
    <l n="18">nostram illam <i>Formam Publicam</i> compo-</l>
    <l n="19">suerunt, qui sanè merito existimen-</l>
    <l n="20">tur ampliori fuisse Gratiâ &amp; Donis in-</l>
    <l n="21">structi, quò maturâ deliberatione,</l>
    <l n="22">&amp; confociatis consiliis, eas <i>Formas</i> precum</l>
    <l n="23">componerent, quæ communibus Ecc-</l>
    <l n="24">lesiæ indigentiis optimè possent com-</l>
    <l n="25">petere, tum Auditorum intellectus in-</l>
    <l n="26">formare, &amp; eam denique fiduciam &amp;</l>
    <l n="27">fervidam mentis intentionem</l>
    <l n="28">(<i>vitam</i> scilicet Precum &amp; <i>Animam</i>, verumque</l>
    <l n="29">Illum quem sic crebro jactant <i>Spiritum</i>)</l>
    <l n="30">fœlicius multo excitare, quàm speran-</l>
    <l n="31">dum sit ab uno homine, quantácunque</l>
    <l n="32">seorsim</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The first word "mula" at the top is a fragment and its start is unclear; marked [?]. The printed text has "Miniftris" followed by a small mark that I did not transcribe. The Greek running head is copied as printed; the Greek letters are read from the scan and should be checked.</notes>
</page>
